How to compile and run the upgraded Smart Glasses HUD Server on Raspberry Pi Zero W:

Option 1 (Using Makefile):
  make
  sudo ./raspberry

Option 2 (Direct GCC command):
  sudo gcc -O2 raspberry.c ssd1306_i2c.c -lwiringPi -lbluetooth -lpthread -o raspberry
  sudo ./raspberry

Optional Audio TTS Package (for WM8960 Audio HAT voice announcements):
  sudo apt-get install espeak alsa-utils

Supported Protocol Commands (over Bluetooth RFCOMM Channel 1, Wi-Fi TCP Port 8888, or local STDIN):
  SYS|<HH:MM>|<Date>|<PhoneBattery%>|<Weather>
  NOTIF|<WHATSAPP/SMS/EMAIL/SOCIAL>|<Sender/Title>|<Message Body>
  NAV|<STRAIGHT/LEFT/RIGHT/SLIGHT_LEFT/SLIGHT_RIGHT/UTURN/ARRIVED>|<Distance>|<Street>|<ETA>
  MUSIC|<PLAY/PAUSE>|<Track Title>|<Artist>|<Progress 0-100>
  CALL|<RINGING/ACTIVE/ENDED>|<Caller Name>|<Phone Number>
  BMP|<2048 hex characters (128x64 1-bit dithered frame)>
  TTS|<Text to speak aloud on WM8960 Audio HAT | ON | OFF>
  MIRROR|<flip_x: 0/1>|<flip_y: 0/1>
  BRIGHTNESS|<0-255>
  MODE|<DASHBOARD|NOTIF|NAV|MUSIC>
  NEXT / PREV / clear
